\noindent\textbf{Supplementary compositional notes:}
\begin{itemize}
\item The Ni-Cr-Mo-V rotor steel (p.\,106) was tested with UTS 882 MPa; balance iron.
\item API-5LX Grade X42 carbon-manganese pipeline steel (p.\,106) was evaluated with UTS 490\textendash{}511 MPa; composition not detailed in the source.
\item Type 304 stainless steel and Mn-Cr austenitic drill collar alloy are referenced (p.\,267); specific compositions not tabulated.
\item 7075-T6 aluminum alloy (p.\,348) was tested with UTS 586 MPa at 600,000 cycles to failure; 2024-T851 alloy referenced for low-cycle fatigue.
\item 7475-T7651 and 7050-T7651 aluminum alloys (p.\,48) are noted for spectrum-loaded fatigue behaviour.
\item 75S-T6 aluminum alloy (p.\,18) is identified as equivalent to modern 7075, used in Zapffe fatigue striation studies.
\item AISI type 304 stainless steel bellows (p.\,624) were examined after H\textsubscript{2} service at 172 kPa.
\item Fe-8Al-6Mo-0.8Zr-0.1C iron-aluminum alloy (p.\,637) exhibited 2\,\% elongation annealed and 19\,\% elongation water quenched.
\item 356.0-T6 cast aluminum alloy carrier tray (p.\,705) showed Cu and Zn above specified limits; 380.0 die cast aluminum wheel (p.\,716) exhibited cold shut defect.
\item 2014-T6 aluminum alloy heat-treated forging (p.\,725) and 2025-T6 aluminum alloy propeller blade at 107 HB (p.\,729) are referenced.
\item 7075-T6 aluminum alloy short-transverse tension-overload fracture (p.\,736) is documented.
\item NS-55 tungsten fibre (125\,$\mu$m diameter) exhibited DBT transition at $\sim$800\textendash{}950\,$^{\circ}$C (p.\,818); 45 vol\,\% tungsten/1010 steel and 45 vol\,\% tungsten/6061 aluminium matrix composites are also referenced.
\item Cu-30Zn brass (p.\,71) is discussed in relation to fracture colour and stress-corrosion cracking in ammonia, nitrates, sulphates, chlorides, and alkaline solutions.
\item Alloy 42 (p.\,848) is paired with oxygen-free copper (UNS C10100) slip ring and pure silver wires of 0.13 mm diameter.
\end{itemize}

