\vspace{0.5em}
\noindent\textbf{Inclusion analysis}

\begin{itemize}
  \item Common inclusion types observed: manganese sulfide (Type II), alumina (Al$_2$O$_3$), calcium-modified duplex sulfide/aluminate inclusions, oxide inclusions (most common butterfly nucleators), softer ductile sulfide inclusions (do not form butterflies), lenticular carbides, spherical primary carbides (M50), copper inclusions (contamination), titanium hydride (Ti-H, at crack tip).
  \item Inclusion control: calcium treatment at 43\,ppm Ca reduces inclusion count and size; desulphurisation to $\leq$0.010\,\% S and shape control minimises Type II MnS and alumina \textit{(p.\,462)}.
\end{itemize}

