  \item Martensite / austenite referenced for 18Ni maraging.
  \item HAZ carbide precipitation concentrated at grain boundaries.
\end{itemize}

\vspace{1em}

\noindent\textbf{Summary of Welding-Related Defect Mechanisms Discussed:}

\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Hot cracking (EBW, Cu contamination)} -- intergranular cracks with grain-boundary Cu film from melted copper backing plate.
  \item \textbf{Hot tears (GMAW HY-80 HAZ)} -- cracks associated with MnS inclusions.
  \item \textbf{Lamellar tearing (multipass welds)} -- steplike cracks parallel to fusion line beneath HAZ; fibrous / woody fracture surfaces; high through-thickness strain from weld shrinkage under high joint restraint.
  \item \textbf{Hydrogen-induced (cold) cracking} -- in weld metal / HAZ.
  \item \textbf{Stress-relief (reheat) cracking} -- intergranular; fine intra-granular carbides with denuded grain boundaries in CrMoV and $2\tfrac{1}{4}$Cr--1Mo steels.
  \item \textbf{Solidification cracking} -- in fully austenitic Cr--Ni stainless weld metals.
  \item \textbf{$475\,^\circ\mathrm{C}$ / $885\,^\circ\mathrm{F}$ embrittlement} -- of ferritic and duplex stainless steels.
\end{itemize}

\noindent Susceptible alloy systems highlighted: HY-80, $2\tfrac{1}{4}$Cr--1Mo, CrMoV, A508 Cl.\,2, A533B, 4340, 18Ni maraging, Cr--Ni austenitic stainless, ferritic and duplex stainless steels.

